From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rdkb-cli: preserve active topology drag

The two-second live topology poll can replace the complete SVG while an
operator is panning the canvas or dragging a node.  The pointer remains down
but its D3 gesture target no longer exists, so movement stops until the next
drag.

Track both zoom and node-drag interactions, retain the latest changed snapshot
while an interaction is active, and apply it after release.  Also reject an
empty snapshot when a valid controller topology is already displayed.  The
controller itself must always be present, and runtime sampling showed these
empty responses to be transient provider delivery misses followed by the full
topology.

